<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply rises in September.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply rises in September.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$466 million to C$63.97 billion in September from C$63.50 billion in August and compared with C$58.36 billion in September 1995, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					  Sept 96     Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.97	63.50	58.36</p>
<p>M2					390.60     389.11     382.89</p>
<p>M3					484.49     482.42     466.11</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			   Sept	   Aug</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-12.32	-11.24</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     653.15	640.42</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.95	102.78</p>
<p>				    Wk to Sept 18 Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.418  +0.080     +0.942</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     7.315  +3.360     -3.826</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	463.946  +2.441     +6.262</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 150.600  -0.300    -17.200</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  29.829  -0.055     +0.694</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
</text>
